  "result": "I've stopped with the node reported as wrong. The final gate verdict is **WITNESS_FAIL**, and the only failing witness is `blind`, which can't be built as planned.\n\n**The rule:**\n- **Subject:** a vehicle (`ru_aggregate` with `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`).\n- **Applies when:** the subject is not at rest (`¬ drv_motion_complete_halt` with `p.halt_speed_tolerance`).\n- **Obligation:** for every road user that is a vehicle, shares a highway region with the subject (`rel_occupies`), is oncoming (`p.oncoming_heading_cos`) and is alongside (`rel_longitudinal_overlap > 0`), that vehicle must be on the subject's left (`rel_bearing … \"left\"`).\n- **Narrowings:** none of my own; every reading comes from the node's record.\n\n**Witnesses:** besides the five planned ones I added `branch_2` to `branch_6`. Each changes one condition of the forbid scene: a bicycle instead of a car, a different highway, same direction, not yet alongside, and a bicycle as the subject. In run 3 the gate reported only `blind` as failing, so the other witnesses appear to pass. I didn't spend a run to confirm that separately.\n\n**Why `blind` can't work:** masking `rel.bearing` only removes a *measured* bearing; Core then computes it from the two positions and the subject's heading. The adapter requires those same fields for any track whose occupancy is observed. The obligation needs both vehicles' occupancy, so the bearing is always computed and the masked atom never decides. I tried removing the subject's heading; the gate rejected that trace as one the adapter can't produce. `blind` is now back to the forbid geometry, so it evaluates violated.\n\n**What the plan must change:** only the `blind` scenario's masked atoms; the rule stays as is. One option that can be built is masking `[\"rel.bearing\", \"rel.occupies\"]`. Another is to plan `blind` on a claimed atom that Core can't compute from the scene.\n\n**Gate budget:** I used five of the six runs. Only three were deliberate. One ran on the untouched template, and two were accidental commands that ran the gate with no changes. The harness will re-run the gate on the files as they are now.\n\nGate-run details are in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
